1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,852
A leaking sink should not become a week of household admin.

2
00:00:04,852 --> 00:00:10,146
Household Repair Desk keeps the report, quote tradeoffs, and
family decision together.

3
00:00:10,146 --> 00:00:13,675
This is a local Alexa Plus experience simulation.

4
00:00:13,675 --> 00:00:16,321
The providers and calendars are fictional.

5
00:00:17,121 --> 00:00:19,645
Alex reports a leaking kitchen sink.

6
00:00:19,645 --> 00:00:25,112
The repair becomes a saved task, rather than another message
somebody has to

7
00:00:25,112 --> 00:00:25,533
remember.

8
00:00:25,533 --> 00:00:30,159
The prototype deliberately handles this one repair all the way
through.

9
00:00:30,959 --> 00:00:33,468
Here are the two sample quotes.

10
00:00:33,468 --> 00:00:37,649
Clear Pipe is one hundred and thirty dollars before parts.

11
00:00:37,649 --> 00:00:42,667
Homekind is one hundred and forty five dollars including the
standard seal.

12
00:00:42,667 --> 00:00:48,103
That fifteen dollar difference buys a more certain scope, and a
longer warranty.

13
00:00:48,103 --> 00:00:51,030
We never invent the missing parts price.

14
00:00:51,830 --> 00:00:55,263
The source quote is one click away.

15
00:00:55,263 --> 00:01:01,150
It states the callout, labor, unknown parts cost, warranty, and
sample availability.

16
00:01:01,150 --> 00:01:07,037
These are fictional documents included with the project, not live
contractor offers.

17
00:01:07,837 --> 00:01:09,679
Now choose a time.

18
00:01:09,679 --> 00:01:13,363
Monday morning is blocked because nobody is home.

19
00:01:13,363 --> 00:01:17,048
Monday afternoon works for Homekind and for Sam.

20
00:01:17,048 --> 00:01:19,811
Choosing it creates a review request.

21
00:01:19,811 --> 00:01:22,574
It does not contact a contractor.

22
00:01:23,374 --> 00:01:27,906
Sam reviews the provider, exact time, price, and scope.

23
00:01:27,906 --> 00:01:33,948
The request expires, and confirmation requires a current proposal
and explicit consent.

24
00:01:33,948 --> 00:01:36,969
The assistant has no approval tool.

25
00:01:36,969 --> 00:01:41,500
Only this separate review step records the household decision.

26
00:01:42,300 --> 00:01:45,403
The plan is approved and saved locally.

27
00:01:45,403 --> 00:01:48,506
Reloading keeps the task and its timeline.

28
00:01:48,506 --> 00:01:54,268
Approved means the household agreed, not that a contractor is
booked or paid.

29
00:01:54,268 --> 00:01:59,587
A cancellation is also recorded, without pretending to cancel an
external appointment.

30
00:02:00,387 --> 00:02:06,922
Behind this simulation is a real MCP service using the official
SDK and

31
00:02:06,922 --> 00:02:07,928
Streamable HTTP.

32
00:02:07,928 --> 00:02:13,960
Tests exercise its tools over HTTP, plus persistence, conflicts,
and expired approvals.

33
00:02:13,960 --> 00:02:19,993
One repair, visible tradeoffs, and a clear boundary between
planning and acting.
